From: YanIanZ <iwayanbagusaryadarma@student.telkomuniversity.ac.id>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 06:09:16 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] SourbyCraft - Aurora wording for the region scheduler start
 line

The engine baseline logs "Initialised EDF Folia scheduler with initial
N target thread(s)" once per boot. Folia is not the product identity
since Build 47, so the line now reads "Initialised Aurora region
scheduler (EDF) with initial N target thread(s)". The scheduler type
and thread count are unchanged; no script or test reads this line.

diff --git a/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/TickRegions.java b/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/TickRegions.java
index 3ac4ab7f6b92e1cb018ef91c3a6f7238b2e48dd0..88b5fb966488ad875edf894e446b67ddbb0f42cb 100644
--- a/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/TickRegions.java
+++ b/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/TickRegions.java
@@ -106,7 +106,7 @@ public final class TickRegions implements ThreadedRegionizer.RegionCallbacks<Tic
         gridExponent = Math.min(31, gridExponent);
         regionShift = gridExponent;
         scheduler = new TickRegionScheduler(config.scheduler, tickThreads);
-        LOGGER.info("Initialised {} Folia scheduler with initial {} target thread(s)", config.scheduler, tickThreads);
+        LOGGER.info("Initialised Aurora region scheduler ({}) with initial {} target thread(s)", config.scheduler, tickThreads); // SourbyCraft - SourbyCraft-owned wording
     }
 
     public static void start() {
